 The list of discovered PuppetDB targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.puppetdbSDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
 
+## scaleway_sd_configs
+
+Scaleway SD configuration allows retrieving scrape targets from [Scaleway](https://www.scaleway.com/) Instances.
+
+Configuration example:
+
+```yaml
+scrape_configs:
+- job_name: scaleway
+  scaleway_sd_configs:
+
+    # project_id is the id of the Scaleway project to discover instances for. This option is required.
+    #
+  - project_id: "..."
+
+    # secret_key is the Scaleway API secret key used for authenticating API requests. This option is required.
+    #
+    secret_key: "..."
+
+    # zone is an optional Scaleway zone to discover instances in.
+    # By default, "fr-par-1" is used.
+    # See https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/api/#region-and-zones
+    #
+    # zone: "fr-par-1"
+
+    # api_url is an optional Scaleway API server to query.
+    # By default, https://api.scaleway.com is used.
+    #
+    # api_url: "https://api.scaleway.com"
+
+    # name_filter is an optional filter for discovering instances with the given name.
+    #
+    # name_filter: "..."
+
+    # tags_filter is an optional filter for discovering instances, which contain all the given tags.
+    #
+    # tags_filter: ["...", "..."]
+
+    # port is an optional port to scrape metrics from. By default, port 80 is used.
+    #
+    # port: ...
+
+    # Additional HTTP API client options can be specified here.
+    # See https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/sd_configs/#http-api-client-options
+```
+
+Each discovered target has an [`__address__`](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/#how-to-modify-scrape-urls-in-targets) label set
+to `<ip>:<port>`, where `<ip>` is the private IPv4 of the instance when available, otherwise the public IPv4, and `<port>` is the port specified in the `scaleway_sd_configs`.
+Instances without a usable IPv4 address are skipped.
+
+The following meta labels are available on discovered targets during [relabeling](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/):
+
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_id`: the id of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_name`: the name of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_hostname`: the hostname of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_type`: the commercial type of the instance (e.g. `DEV1-S`)
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_status`: the status of the instance (e.g. `running`, `stopped`) — use this for [relabeling](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/) if only running instances should be scraped
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_boot_type`: the boot type of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_zone`: the zone the instance is running in
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_region`: the region the instance is running in (the zone with the trailing `-N` suffix stripped)
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_organization_id`: the id of the organization the instance belongs to
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_project_id`: the id of the project the instance belongs to
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_private_ipv4`: the private IPv4 of the instance, if present
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ipv4`: the public IPv4 of the instance, if present
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_image_id`: the id of the instance's image, if present
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_image_name`: the name of the instance's image, if present
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_image_arch`: the architecture of the instance's image, if present
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_security_group_id`: the id of the instance's security group, if present
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_security_group_name`: the name of the instance's security group, if present
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_tags`: a comma separated list of tags of the instance
+
+The list of discovered Scaleway targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.scalewaySDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
+
 ## static_configs
 
 A static config allows specifying a list of targets and a common label set for them.
